<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#191a18"><title>Mars Field Trip — The surface is yours to explore</title>
<meta name="description" content="Explore Mars, collect geological samples and run science experiments with a voiced guide. Free browser access on desktop, mobile and Meta Quest.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css?v=16"><script src="aframe.min.js"></script><script src="core.js?v=16"></script><script src="journey-core.js?v=16"></script><script src="voice-lines.js?v=16"></script><script src="app.js?v=16"></script><script src="exploration.js?v=16"></script><script src="landscape.js?v=16"></script><script src="sound-map.js?v=16"></script><script src="dust-science.js?v=16"></script><script src="comfort.js?v=16"></script><script src="journey.js?v=16"></script><script src="flight-polish.js?v=16"></script>
</head><body>
<div id="loading" role="status"><span class="loading-orbit"></span><b>Preparing your landing</b><span id="load-status">Loading the Mars surface…</span><button id="reload" hidden onclick="location.reload()">Reload expedition</button></div>
<a-scene id="world" renderer="antialias: true; colorManagement: true; foveationLevel: 0.5; maxCanvasWidth: 2048; maxCanvasHeight: 2048" shadow="type: pcfsoft" background="color: #b49b82" xr-mode-ui="enabled: false" webxr="referenceSpaceType: local-floor" mars-expedition>
<a-entity id="land"></a-entity><a-entity id="stations"></a-entity><a-entity id="vr-ui"></a-entity>
<a-entity id="rig"><a-camera id="head" position="0 1.65 0" fov="72" near="0.05" far="700" wasd-controls="enabled: false" look-controls="pointerLockEnabled: false; touchEnabled: true"></a-camera><a-entity id="left-hand" laser-controls="hand: left; model: false" raycaster="objects: .target; far: 9; lineColor: #c4e7d4; lineOpacity: 0.7"></a-entity><a-entity id="right-hand" laser-controls="hand: right; model: false" raycaster="objects: .target; far: 9; lineColor: #c4e7d4; lineOpacity: 0.7"></a-entity></a-entity>
</a-scene>
<div id="screen-ui"><section id="arrival" hidden></section><section id="journey-hud" aria-label="Earth to Mars journey"><div class="journey-heading"><span>ARES 01 · EARTH LAUNCH SITE</span><h1>Next stop: Mars.</h1><p id="journey-status" role="status">Your expedition begins on Earth.</p></div><div id="journey-options"><button data-journey="tutorial" class="primary">Quick tutorial</button><button data-journey="launch">Walk to the rocket</button><button data-journey="skip">Skip to Mars</button><p>Choose the tutorial to learn movement, selection and controller shortcuts.</p></div><div id="tutorial-panel" hidden><h2 id="tutorial-title"></h2><p id="tutorial-copy"></p><button id="tutorial-next" class="primary">Next step</button></div><button id="journey-board" hidden>Board rocket · Enter</button><div class="journey-bottom"><span>Illustrative journey · months compressed into one minute</span><button id="journey-sound">Sound on</button><button id="journey-skip">Skip journey</button></div><div class="journey-track"><span id="journey-progress"></span></div></section>
<header class="topbar"><a class="brand" href="./" aria-label="Mars Field Trip home"><span class="brand-mark">M</span><span>MARS<span class="brand-sub">FIELD TRIP</span></span></a><nav aria-label="Expedition stations" id="station-nav"><button data-station="0" aria-current="page"><span>00</span> Base camp</button><button data-station="1"><span>01</span> Rock field</button><button data-station="2"><span>02</span> Gravity lab</button><button data-station="3"><span>03</span> Challenge</button></nav><button id="vr" class="primary" disabled>Checking VR…</button></header>
<div id="explore-status"><span id="zone-state">FREE EXPLORATION</span><span id="field-position"></span><button id="leave-mission" hidden>Stop mission / walk</button></div><aside id="map-panel" aria-label="Field minimap"><canvas id="minimap" width="256" height="256" role="img" aria-label="North-up map showing your position, rover, five mission areas and the field boundary"></canvas><span>You ▲ · Rover ▪ · Missions 1–5</span></aside><div id="movement-pad" aria-label="Movement controls"><span id="move-label">WALK</span><button data-move="KeyW" aria-label="Move forward">↑</button><div><button data-move="KeyA" aria-label="Move left or steer left">←</button><button data-move="KeyS" aria-label="Move backward">↓</button><button data-move="KeyD" aria-label="Move right or steer right">→</button></div></div><div class="location"><span class="eyebrow">SURFACE EXPEDITION</span><h1 id="location">Base camp</h1><p id="location-note">A new perspective on the Red Planet.</p></div>
<div class="view-tools"><button id="recenter" title="Face your current station">⌖ Recenter</button><button id="missions-toggle" aria-expanded="false">Missions</button><button id="effects-toggle" aria-pressed="true">Ambience on</button><button id="guide-toggle" aria-expanded="false">Guide</button><button id="station-tour">Outpost</button><button id="rover-tab">Rover</button><button id="dust-travel">Dust lab</button><button id="tutorial-replay">Tutorial</button><button id="help">Controls</button><button id="hide-ui" aria-label="Hide panels for an unobstructed view" aria-pressed="false">Clear view</button></div>
<main class="mission-card" id="mission-card"><div class="card-top"><span class="eyebrow" id="mission-label">MISSION CONTROL</span><span class="mission-score" id="count">0 / 3 complete</span></div><div class="progress" role="progressbar" aria-label="Completed missions" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="3" aria-valuenow="0"><span id="progress"></span></div><h2 id="task-title">Make your first discovery.</h2><p id="task-description">Three hands-on missions. One extraordinary world. Choose a station to begin.</p><div id="task-actions"></div><p id="feedback" role="status"></p><div class="card-footer"><span id="sample-count">0 / 3 samples</span><button id="restart">↻ Restart</button></div></main>
<section class="guide" aria-label="NOVA voice guide"><button id="voice" aria-label="Start voice guide" class="voice-orb">▷</button><div class="guide-copy"><div class="guide-top"><span class="eyebrow">NOVA <span>FIELD GUIDE</span></span><div class="voice-actions"><button id="replay" aria-label="Replay narration">Replay</button><button id="mute" aria-label="Mute narration" aria-pressed="false">Sound on</button></div></div><p id="caption" aria-live="polite">Welcome, explorer. Start the voice guide or choose your first mission.</p></div></section>
<footer><span id="controls-hint">WASD / arrows: walk · Drag: look · Enter a circle: start mission</span><a id="credits-link" href="https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-perseverance-rover-3d-model/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Model: NASA/JPL-Caltech ↗</a></footer>
</div>
<button id="restore-ui" hidden>Show controls</button><div id="notice" role="status" hidden></div>
<dialog id="help-dialog"><form method="dialog"><button class="close" aria-label="Close controls">×</button><span class="eyebrow">EXPEDITION CONTROLS</span><h2>Your field manual</h2><h3>Earth to Mars</h3><p>At startup choose Quick tutorial, Walk to the rocket or Skip to Mars. Follow the launchpad markings and enter the rocket’s front doorway to board the cabin and close its hatch before the countdown. Enter or Board rocket follows the boarding path automatically. The flight includes ascent, Earth orbit, interplanetary transfer, atmospheric entry and powered descent. The cabin stays stable without forced head rotation. Skip journey or B in VR jumps straight to the field. This is a fictional, time-compressed journey.</p><h3>Visible controllers</h3><p>In VR, both controllers have visible simplified bodies, thumbsticks, triggers and labelled face buttons. Sticks and buttons animate with input. The tutorial explains controls in four short steps; use the trigger to select Next step.</p><h3>Desktop & mobile</h3><p>Use WASD, arrow keys or the movement pad to walk. Drag the landscape to look around. Station tabs and keys 1–4 take you outside each start circle. Walk into a glowing circle to start its mission. The Rover button takes you to rover control. Approach and select a rock to scan it; stay nearby until scanning finishes.</p><h3>Meta Quest</h3><p>Open this page directly in Meta Quest Browser and choose Enter VR. Point a controller ray and press the trigger to interact. Use the left thumbstick to walk; right thumbstick left/right turns in 30° steps. The panel changes destinations. Walk into a glowing circle to start. In the rover circle, the left stick drives and steers the rover; use Release rover controls to walk again. No sign-in is needed.</p><h3>Exploring the outpost</h3><p>Choose Outpost to visit the habitat exterior, solar arrays and communications equipment. Missions opens your task list; Guide expands voice controls and captions. The ridges and valleys use different surface textures while activity areas stay level.</p><h3>Earth vs Mars dust lab</h3><p>Enter the Dust lab circle. Compare Earth and Mars at the same 20 m/s wind speed. This example uses air densities of 1.2 and 0.02 kg/m³: dynamic pressure q = ½ρv² gives 240 Pa on Earth and 4 Pa on Mars. These are example conditions, not fixed planetary constants. The chamber particles trace airflow; they do not predict dust-lifting thresholds or settling times.</p><p>Next, start a Mars dust storm. Clean the panel, then clear the sky. Cleaning removes deposited dust but cannot remove dust overhead. The teaching model assigns 35% light transmission to a dusty sky and 50% transmission to a coated panel; output is their product, relative to the same planet’s clean baseline. These percentages are illustrative, not rover measurements or an Earth–Mars solar-flux comparison. The sky and coating stay dusty after Stop wind. Leaving the activity stops its wind.</p><p>Earth also has dust storms. Mars has thin air, a dry dusty surface and storms that can spread globally. Solar-powered Opportunity lost contact during the 2018 global dust storm. Perseverance uses a radioisotope power source, so this panel demonstration represents solar-powered missions, not its main power supply. <a href="https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/the-fact-and-fiction-of-martian-dust-storms/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NASA: Martian dust storms</a> · <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/dusty-differences-between-mars-and-earth-149926/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NASA: Earth and Mars comparison</a></p><h3>Sound & map</h3><p>Ambience controls the wind, footsteps and rover sounds separately from the guide. Audio begins after your first interaction, softens during narration, and pauses when you leave the tab. Surface ambience and landing thrusters are designed simulation sounds. Launch uses NASA’s real Atlas V recording, adapted to this fictional flight. No sound travels through the vacuum outside the cabin. The north-up minimap shows you in white, the rover in blue, missions 1–5 and the field perimeter. The dotted line points toward your selected mission. In VR, press X to open the compact menu and left-controller map. Press X again to clear the view. Y toggles small captions, A replays the guide and B stops the current mission. Menus and captions start hidden. When opened, they follow your head position and viewing direction. The tutorial and flight instructions also follow you in VR. Object labels stay with their objects.</p><h3>Flight audio</h3><p>Launch recording: <a href="https://www.nasa.gov/historical-sounds/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NASA, Atlas V: Launch</a>. Landing effects are simulated, not a Mars touchdown recording. NASA’s Perseverance microphone did not capture its descent. Use Ambience to mute effects. Journey time and vehicle design are illustrative.</p><h3>Guide & comfort</h3><p>Nova uses one consistent AI-generated English voice throughout the expedition. All guide recordings are bundled with the site.</p><p>Start the guide once to enable narration. Replay and mute are always available. Travel moves you to a station approach. Recenter faces forward without moving you. The amber outer perimeter limits field travel. Each mission has a smaller marked area: leaving it stops narration and cancels unfinished progress; completed missions are kept. In rover control, drive through the three numbered markers in order inside the blue course boundary. Press E or Stop mission to return to walking.</p><p class="muted">This is an educational simulation. The sky and landscape are a continuous 3D educational simulation, not a surveyed Mars landing site. Rover: NASA/JPL-Caltech. Ground and hill textures: Poly Haven, CC0. Clouds are subtle illustrative high-altitude wisps. Test tube: Jakob Hippe, CC BY 3.0; liquid removed and glass adapted for the vacuum experiment.</p><p class="muted"><a href="https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-perseverance-rover-3d-model/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NASA Perseverance model</a> · <a href="https://polyhaven.com/a/rocky_trail_02" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Poly Haven ground texture</a> · <a href="https://polyhaven.com/a/cliff_side" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Poly Haven hill texture</a> · Planet textures: <a href="https://www.solarsystemscope.com/textures/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Solar System Scope</a> (<a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>) · <a href="https://poly.pizza/m/1F33UFXOEau" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Test tube by Jakob Hippe</a> (<a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY 3.0</a>)</p><button class="primary">Back to Mars</button></form></dialog>
<dialog id="reset-dialog"><form method="dialog"><h2>Start a new expedition?</h2><p>This clears the samples, experiment and quiz for the next student.</p><div class="dialog-actions"><button value="cancel">Keep exploring</button><button id="confirm-reset" value="reset" class="primary">Restart</button></div></form></dialog>
<noscript>This experience needs JavaScript. Enable it and reload the page.</noscript>
</body></html>
